add('lesson:'+web,'Navigation container connecting browser execution, human deception, registrar/name-resolution trust and protected error handling.',['Profile title/summary replace the authored header; phishing and DNS filtering have keyword definitions but limited developed lesson treatment.','No complete objective2.2/2.3/2.4 coverage, implemented defense or observed recovery.','Stored/reflected persistence can coexist with DOM execution. Safe display here is not general application security.'],['xss','csrf','dns','pretexting']);
add('keywords:'+web,'Three-entry guide for browser-script execution, deceptive messages and DNS-policy filtering.',['The guide mixes attacks with a defensive control; DNS filtering does not authenticate DNS data, replace secure output sinks or guarantee all malicious destinations are blocked.','Whole-guide references do not map each generated response to an assessed concept.'],guideLinks[0]);
add('traps:'+web,'Qualified comparisons of primary XSS controls versus defense in depth, registrar control versus DNS integrity, and script execution versus request intent.',['CSP/WAF capabilities depend on policy and visibility; no universal prevention promise.','The authenticated-request shorthand does not exclude login/client-side CSRF or remove credential-eligibility and request-intent premises.'],['xss','csrf','dns']);
add('check:'+web,'Reveal-only stored-XSS persistence example for later viewers.',['Persistence is supported by the saved-content premise; DOM processing can coexist and no execution-sink subtype is uniquely established.','The control reveals text, accepts no response and grades nothing; repeated reveal is not an assessment or repair.'],['xss']);
add('section:'+web+':0','Distinguish persistence/delivery from browser execution and explain safe text output, safe sinks and layered defenses.',['The subtype-overlap sentence and most defenses are initially collapsed; first-sentence exposure alone is incomplete teaching.','No payload executes, no application defense is tested, and React text escaping does not certify arbitrary raw HTML, URLs, attributes or unsafe sinks.','Cookie access and data theft depend on context; not every XSS reads cookies and no outcome is observed.'],['xss']);
add('section:'+web+':1','Four comparison rows separate pretexts, registrar takeover, DNS integrity attacks and forged browser-request intent.',['These are distinct trust boundaries, not unique actor attribution or four independent assessment families.','DNSSEC needs a validating chain; it provides neither DNS confidentiality nor automatic trustworthy site content.','CSRF defenses need token/origin/cookie/action premises; SameSite is not universally sufficient. Registrar recovery and locks depend on provider implementation.'],['pretexting','dns','dnssec','csrf']);
add('section:'+web+':2','Avoid diagnostic data in public responses while keeping protected internal logs and correlation context.',['The safe-message/logging distinction is in collapsed supporting detail; generic errors alone do not repair a vulnerability.','No log access policy, exception handler or diagnostic retention is implemented or tested; exact canonical error-handling identity remains withheld.']);
add('lesson:'+wifi,'Navigation container separating access authentication, data protection and wireless exposure/attack context.',['Domain4 is derived from the first profile objective;2.2/3.2 are broad additional observations, not every child scope.','The supplied NIST800-97 reference is withdrawn; no current secure-design certification or PMF implementation is inferred.','Preserve the deferred check and WPA3-practice row despite useful surrounding instruction.'],['802-1x','ccmp','eap','psk','radius','wpa3']);
add('keywords:'+wifi,'Four-entry guide with useful 802.1X access-control, RADIUS AAA and CCMP traffic-protection summaries, plus a shallow WPA3 label.',['The WPA3 entry names an exam standard but lacks SAE/enterprise/management-protection distinctions; keep that entry limited and its generated exercise deferred.','CCMP is displayed as the fourth guide item but is outside the first three generated keyword checks.','Whole-guide context is not a keyed assessment map.'],guideLinks[1]);
add('traps:'+wifi,'Distinguish access models from frame protection, SAE personal versus enterprise authentication, and identifiers/allowlists from strong authentication.',['An identifier or address allowlist does not authenticate an AP/client; non-broadcast SSIDs still exist and may be disclosed.','WPA3/802.1X is not segmentation, verified authorization policy, perfect availability or protection of every frame.'],['802-1x','ccmp','psk','wpa3']);
add('check:'+wifi,'Individual enterprise identities are useful, but the request for immediate revocation is not fully supported by the model response.',['ZERO CREDIT: identity/account revocation can prevent future authentication without immediately terminating an established session.','The response omits active-session disconnect, reauthentication, cached authorization and implementation premises. RFC5176 describes a separate session-termination mechanism; it is not delivered teaching here.','No raw answer, response-linked concept assignment, trusted grading or new teaching approval is exported.'],[],true);
